## Solution

**Setup and reformulation.** A machine placed at point $P$ punches out every point $Q$ with $|PQ|$ irrational. A point $Q$ is *not* punched by a collection of machines at $P_1,\dots,P_n$ iff $|QP_i|\in\mathbb{Q}_{\ge 0}$ for every $i$. We want to place machines so that **no** point survives, i.e. every point of the plane is at irrational (positive) distance from at least one machine.

---

### Lower bound: 2 machines do not suffice

Place two machines at $P_1,P_2$ with $|P_1P_2|=d\ge 0$.

- If $d=0$: this is just one machine; its own location (distance $0$) is not punched.
- If $d\in\mathbb{Q}_{>0}$: the point $P_1$ itself is at distance $0$ from $P_1$ and distance $d$ from $P_2$, both rational, so $P_1$ is not punched.
